'''Sloth''' is a [[mini-boss]] and one of the [[Seven Deadly Sins]].

== Behavior ==
Sloth wanders randomly around the room and performs one of two attacks:
* Fires an {{i|Ipecac}} projectile in Isaac's direction.
* Spawns a {{e|Charger}} charging in the horizontal direction Sloth is facing before returning to normal Charger patterns.
Sloth deals a whole heart of contact damage.

== Notes ==
* Sloth is often encountered with either 2 {{e|Splasher}}s, 2 {{e|Charger}}s, or 2 {{e|Attack Fly||Attack Flies}}.
* {{dlc|nr}} Sloth can drop {{i|Bob's Rotten Head}} even if Isaac has already encountered/possessed it. 

== Unlockable [[Achievement]]s ==
{{achievement text | The Book of Sin }}

== Trivia ==
* According to Edmund McMillen, Sloth's first name is Bob, and Sloth is his last name. His first name is referenced by the items {{i|Bob's Rotten Head}}, {{i|Bob's Curse}} and {{i|Bob's Brain}}, and is also referenced by the {{tf|Bob}} transformation.
** Furthermore, Edmund confirmed that Bob is [https://twitter.com/edmundmcmillen/status/1218023840145534978?s=21 Isaac’s father’s brother], which makes Bob Isaac’s uncle.
*** This may possibly be just a joke based on the phrase "Bob's your uncle".
* Sloth's sprite is just a re-coloring of the {{e|Globin}} enemy. This may have been done humorously to match his sin, Sloth (laziness).
* The [[wikipedia:Seven Deadly Sins|Seven Deadly Sins]] that these mini-bosses are based upon are, in Christian teachings, a classification of vices from which all others are derived from.
* Sloth is a personification of one of the Seven Deadly Sins. Sloth is an excessive aversion towards difficulty in regards towards doing good, or moral/spiritual laziness. It is believed to lead to negligence, idleness, spite towards those who do good, despair, and other capital sins such as gluttony and lust.

